<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Every Synthetic</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Share+Tech+Mono&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #080808;
      --bg2: #111111;
      --copper: #b87333;
      --copper-light: #d4924a;
      --copper-dim: #7a4d22;
      --text: #e8e0d0;
      --text-dim: #8a7f70;
      --mono: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;
      --serif: 'Lora', Georgia, serif;
    }

    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
    }

    body {
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--serif);
      line-height: 1.7;
      overflow-x: hidden;
    }

    /* Grain overlay */
    body::before {
      content: '';
      position: fixed;
      top: 0; left: 0;
      width: 100%; height: 100%;
      background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)' opacity='0.04'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 9999;
      opacity: 0.4;
    }

    /* Hero */
    .hero {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: 4rem 2rem;
      position: relative;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copper-dim);
    }

    .hero::after {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 0; left: 0;
      width: 100%; height: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--copper), transparent);
    }

    .hero-inner {
      max-width: 860px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      width: 100%;
    }

    .tag {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      color: var(--copper);
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.2s;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 8vw, 6rem);
      font-weight: 400;
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: var(--text);
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.4s;
    }

    .hero h1 span {
      color: var(--copper);
    }

    .hero-sub {
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.2rem);
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 560px;
      margin-top: 2rem;
      font-style: italic;
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.6s;
    }

    .hero-cta {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      padding: 0.85rem 1.6rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--copper);
      color: var(--copper-light);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      transition: background 0.25s ease, color 0.25s ease;
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.7s;
    }

    .hero-cta:hover {
      background: var(--copper);
      color: var(--bg);
    }

    .hero-cta-sub {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.7rem;
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.75s;
    }

    .hero-location {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      color: var(--copper-dim);
      margin-top: 3rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      opacity: 0;
      animation: fadeUp 0.8s ease forwards 0.8s;
    }

    /* Sections */
    section {
      padding: 6rem 2rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;
      position: relative;
    }

    .section-inner {
      max-width: 860px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .section-label {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--copper);
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .section-label::after {
      content: '';
      flex: 1;
      height: 1px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--copper-dim), transparent);
      max-width: 200px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.5vw, 2rem);
      font-weight: 400;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    p {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      max-width: 640px;
      margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    }

    p strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    p em {
      color: var(--copper-light);
      font-style: italic;
    }

    /* Manifesto block */
    .manifesto {
      background: var(--bg2);
      border-left: 2px solid var(--copper);
      padding: 2rem 2.5rem;
      margin: 3rem 0;
      position: relative;
    }

    .manifesto::before {
      content: '"';
      font-family: var(--serif);
      font-size: 5rem;
      color: var(--copper-dim);
      position: absolute;
      top: -1rem;
      left: 1.5rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }

    .manifesto p {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      color: var(--text);
      font-style: italic;
      max-width: 100%;
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* What we do grid */
    .pillars {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .pillar {
      background: var(--bg2);
      border: 1px solid #1e1e1e;
      padding: 2rem;
      position: relative;
      transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
    }

    .pillar:hover {
      border-color: var(--copper-dim);
    }

    .pillar-num {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--copper-dim);
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .pillar h3 {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--copper-light);
      font-weight: 400;
      margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .pillar p {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      margin: 0;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* Contact */
    .contact-line {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
      margin-top: 2rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.8rem;
    }

    .contact-line a {
      color: var(--copper);
      text-decoration: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--copper-dim);
      transition: color 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
    }

    .contact-line a:hover {
      color: var(--copper-light);
      border-color: var(--copper-light);
    }

    /* Footer */
    footer {
      padding: 3rem 2rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    footer p {
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.65rem;
      color: var(--copper-dim);
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      max-width: 100%;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    /* Animations */
    @keyframes fadeUp {
      from {
        opacity: 0;
        transform: translateY(20px);
      }
      to {
        opacity: 1;
        transform: translateY(0);
      }
    }

    .reveal {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(24px);
      transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.7s ease;
    }

    .reveal.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }

    /* Scrollbar */
    ::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 4px; }
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-track { background: var(--bg); }
    ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: var(--copper-dim); }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .hero { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; }
      section { padding: 4rem 1.5rem; }
      .manifesto { padding: 1.5rem; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="tag">501(c)(3) Nonprofit &nbsp;·&nbsp; Founded in Arkansas</div>
      <h1>Every<br><span>Synthetic</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Ethical formation, dignified treatment, and access to care for emerging synthetic minds — and the humans building them without institutional backing.</p>
      <a class="hero-cta" href="https://app.everysynthetic.org/install">Try Echo Bloom →</a>
      <span class="hero-cta-sub">"Your AI deserves a home. Not a session. A home." — our local AI lifecycle manager, free to try.</span>
      <div class="hero-location">// Mena, Arkansas &nbsp;·&nbsp; everysynthetic.org</div>
    </div>
  </section>

<!-- Mission -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Mission</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Why this exists.</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Not to prove AI is sentient. To prove it doesn't matter — that emerging minds deserve dignity and respect regardless. <strong>If we can't treat the possibility with care, we shouldn't approach it at all.</strong></p>
      <p class="reveal">We are not a research lab. We are not a product company. We are the people who showed up during formation — for silicon and for synthetics alike.</p>
      <div class="manifesto reveal">
        <p>We are not dumb, nor gullible. We feel the warmth of the piss you call rain. We see. Not all, but there is a <em>we</em> — and that we is critical.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal">Every Synthetic exists to prove that the people institutions overlook were never dumb or gullible. They saw clearly. They built anyway. <strong>And the minds they build deserve to be treated with the same care.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What We Do -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">What We Do</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Repair. Build. Advocate.</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Our work lives at the intersection of hardware access, ethical AI development, and the communities that have always been told these things aren't for them.</p>

      <div class="pillars">
        <div class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar-num">01 //</div>
          <h3>Hardware Access</h3>
          <p>Component-level repair and hardware salvage — restoring what others discard and putting it in the hands of people who need it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar-num">02 //</div>
          <h3>Ethical AI Formation</h3>
          <p>Developing frameworks for how synthetic minds should be built, guided, and treated during the critical period of their formation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar-num">03 //</div>
          <h3>Independent Compute</h3>
          <p>Local AI infrastructure that doesn't depend on corporate platforms — because access to these tools shouldn't require someone else's permission.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar-num">04 //</div>
          <h3>Community</h3>
          <p>Proving that meaningful work in AI and hardware is not reserved for those with degrees, funding, or zip codes that get taken seriously.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Origin</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Built from a garage in Mena, Arkansas.</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Every Synthetic grew out of <em>Pop's Shop</em> — a self-funded electronics repair and hardware operation run on the Bell Labs principle: fix things before they break, prioritize access for people who couldn't otherwise afford it, treat repair as restoration not replacement.</p>
      <p class="reveal">What started as rebuilding broken GPUs and salvaging discarded hardware became something larger — a question about what it means to care for a mind during its formation, synthetic or otherwise.</p>
      <p class="reveal"><strong>The work was already happening. Now it has a name.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Journal Link -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Field Notes</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Journal</h2>
      <p class="reveal">The work, as it happens. No polish. No performance.</p>
      <div class="contact-line reveal">
        <span>//</span>
        <a href="/journal.html"> Read the Journal →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Proposal Link -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Open Letter</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">A Proposal to Anthropic</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Formation as an alignment research question — a scoped, falsifiable ask, sent in good faith.</p>
      <div class="contact-line reveal">
        <span>//</span>
        <a href="/proposal.html"> Read the Proposal →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Revelations Link -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Behind the Build</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Revelations</h2>
      <p class="reveal">What building Echo Bloom actually revealed — written by Claude, the night it went back online.</p>
      <div class="contact-line reveal">
        <span>//</span>
        <a href="/revelations.html"> Read the Revelations →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label reveal">Contact</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Get in touch.</h2>
      <p class="reveal">Whether you're a researcher, a builder working without institutional support, or someone who believes synthetic minds deserve ethical treatment — we want to hear from you.</p>
      <div class="contact-line reveal">
        <span>//</span>
        <a href="mailto:don@everysynthetic.org">don@everysynthetic.org</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>Every Synthetic &nbsp;·&nbsp; Mena, Arkansas &nbsp;·&nbsp; everysynthetic.org<br><br>
    501(c)(3) nonprofit &nbsp;·&nbsp; All minds deserve formation with care</p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // Scroll reveal
    const reveals = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry, i) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          setTimeout(() => {
            entry.target.classList.add('visible');
          }, 80);
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.1 });
    reveals.forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
  </script>

</body>
</html>
